WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:05.000
When Takuya Beast Spirit evolved to Burning Greymon, he couldn't control himself at all.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.700
So Beetlemon and Kendogorurumon tried to help him, but they were pretty useless.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.980
It finally took a lot of reasoning from little Tommy to get Takuya to tame the beast within.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.180
Then it was off to the forest terminal again.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.880
But when the gang got stuck in the mud, Grumblemon showed up and grabbed Tommy.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.460
So Takuya Beast Spirit evolved and did a little grabbing of his own.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.460
He took Giggismon's spirit and returned Kumomons to Tommy.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.540
But Grumblemon escaped and met up with the evil legendary warriors.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.940
Man, those are some...

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:29.960
Thank you.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:43.500
Past and fortune to reclaim gentle words

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.560
Faith in ourselves, trust in each other

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:58.860
We live through a speed

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.350
Hey, where do you think you're going? Mercury Mon ain't done with you yet.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:43.350
I'm going forest terminal. Must get B-spirit back from annoying kids.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.620
Eww, sounds like fun.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.210
I tried to stop him. You saw, right?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.120
Please be my brethren.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.130
I can't believe it. We're actually here.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.810
My legs can believe it.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.480
There's the sign, Forest Terminal.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.270
Um, but shouldn't there be a Trailmon here?

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.270
Yeah, really.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:16.020
Huh?

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.010
Well, maybe they're on their way back right now.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.560
Or, uh, you know, they, uh, could be...

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.380
Oh, man.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:24.290
Hm?

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.040
Hey, who cares about the Trailmon? There's a restaurant here!

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.100
Welcome, weary travelers.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.760
What do you have to eat?

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.080
Ask instead what I don't have to eat.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.880
Step right up, friends, and don't worry about money.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.440
For you, the first meal is free.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:43.570
Hey!

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.740
Now there's a man who knows what he likes

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.060
and doesn't care what he eats.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.880
Yolk Surprise coming up!

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:58.500
To the chef!

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:10.920
We must respectfully decline your kind offer of food.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.260
You're my tongue anymore.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.900
All right, all right. What's the big idea?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.660
I just can't believe all of you are going to turn down free food.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:21.920
That was food.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:23.410
I'm insulted.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.260
I'm going to be sick.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.520
Fine. Get out of here, kid. You're bugging me.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.140
Go on and go to the forest terminal.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.170
They say no one's ever returned from there.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.760
Yeah, well, we'll just take our chances.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.660
I doubt the forest terminal will be any worse than this food.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.130
Aw, come on, guys.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.270
I was just trying to be nice, that's all.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.520
Being nice has nothing to do with cooking.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.420
And rumors don't matter to us.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.000
We've already been told that we have to go to the forest terminal.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:53.690
Attention.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.870
Go to the forest terminal immediately.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:02.900
Let's go.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:08.180
Do you think it's dangerous?

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:09.080
I don't know.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:09.920
We've come this far.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.900
We can't turn back.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:12.340
Huh?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.140
I mean, wait up.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.900
This place is empty, too.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.900
Yeah, and just a little bit creepy.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.150
Your eyes peel, guys.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.030
For what?

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.430
All we can see is fog.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.010
Well, there have to be some people here.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:29.970
But what if they're all...

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:37.920
ghosts I guess we have no choice but to keep walking and this world sure loves

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:56.720
its walking great now what that way are you sure it wasn't the other way

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:15.300
For my next trick, man. I can't see anything in this fog. I know we could be attacked. Maybe my detectors good for something, too

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.980
This place is beautiful.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.800
Doesn't mean it's not dangerous.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.160
What if this is where the person from our detector lives?

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.680
We did get a message to come here.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:38.960
Well, should I knock?

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.460
I still don't think it's safe.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:51.280
Well, at least they're polite, I guess.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.480
Yeah, that or eager to lure us in there.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.700
Here we go inside.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.000
How could it be?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.960
Sleeping Beauty used to live in a castle in...

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.580
Yeah, well, so did the Wicked Witch.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.020
We'll never find out what's in there if we don't go in.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:07.020
Says the kid at the back of the line.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.310
Maybe no one lives here.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:13.130
Maybe you should open up a wishful thinking store, Tommy.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.230
Back to Rubimonskami.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.270
Uh, isn't that Wizardmon?

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.040
He's a different color.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:24.110
And meaner.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.950
We can beat him just like we beat Giggismon.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:27.880
Giggismon?

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.760
But he's one of Cherubimons goons.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.400
Yeah.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:33.700
So you're not allies with Cherubimon.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.020
Are you kidding?

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.460
Look, why don't you put that wand down, okay?

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.180
We're all on the same side. Isn't that obvious?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.100
This is what comes of fighting too much.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.600
Everyone seems to be an enemy.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.140
I apologize, friends.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.940
How did you find this place?

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.400
We got a message that told us all to come to the forest terminal.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.800
But there was no one there, and when we kept walking, we ended up here on your doorstep.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.590
Ah, a message. Could it be?

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:03.130
My solitude is driven common courtesy from me. I apologize.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:07.570
My name is Sorcerer Mon. Please, come in. I have something important to show you.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.640
Whatever did I do wrong?

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.750
The recipe's clear. One egg and pasta, boiled in dirty socks.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.940
Aha! Welcome, travelers. Your first meal is free.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.160
To forest terminal. It'll be easier than I thought.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.620
Where are you taking us, anyway?

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.250
To meet someone. I bet it's a trap.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.950
You think everything's a trap.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.570
Caution is wise, friends, but only within reason.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.140
This is no trap. This is a prophecy.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.480
Go further.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:51.940
So where is he?

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:52.700
Up there.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:53.410
Huh?

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.420
Allow me to introduce our salvation, Seraphimon.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.220
Um, are we supposed to know who that is?

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:07.490
Seraphimon was one of the three celestial Digimon chosen to rule this world.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:11.640
So what are we supposed to do? He's all frozen up.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.140
Perhaps not for long. There is a prophecy.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.200
Let your light shine as wine.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:20.740
That was Lady Ophanimon. She's the one who asked me to watch over Seraphimon.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.130
Ophanimon? She must be the voice that told us to come here.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.890
It's all falling into place.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.970
I brought you here because the prophecy says that one day a group...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.160
of wayward humans will free Serafimon.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.130
Typical. Humans get to do everything.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.610
When is my turn?

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:37.950
How about next week?

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:38.870
Be quiet.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:40.310
Just little further.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:41.750
So you keep saying.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:43.330
So what did she mean?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:47.130
Hey, I bet it has something to do with our detectors.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:48.450
Huh?

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:49.210
Oh.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:49.750
Huh?

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.030
Whoa!

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:55.500
Guys, focus them up there!

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:06.220
Prophecy? Welcome back, Lord Sarathemon.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.250
It's good to be back, faithful servant. You have done well.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:11.600
Little further.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:12.880
Will you stop that?

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.950
Sorceremon, tell me. There's so little I remember.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.520
My lord, when your defeat seemed imminent, Ophanimon was able to get you to safety.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:25.210
She sealed you away from danger so you could be revived after the trouble had passed.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.850
Ophanimon, that's right. Has she been harmed? Why isn't she here?

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.140
Truth is often unpleasant, I'm afraid.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.680
No one knows where she is.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.420
But these humans have been in contact with her, so all is not lost.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:38.980
These humans?

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.980
But they're only children.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.450
Yes, but they're also legendary warriors,

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.950
and if not for them, you'd still be stuck to the ceiling.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.610
Legendary warriors? Impressive.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.440
Hey, listen, just what is going on here?

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.960
We've been led all over, getting our snot kicked out,

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.940
and we don't even know why we were brought into this crazy world.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.220
Yeah, someone owes us some answers.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.950
And I think you're that someone. So tell us what's going on.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.580
Um, please?

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.020
Very well, brave ones. I shall tell you.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.720
No little further. We here now.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.900
What a delightful place to destroy those kitties.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.320
They won't know what hit them, right, Mercury Mon?

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:18.660
They shall know pain. That I promise.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.400
If you want answers, you will have them.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.320
The story begins long ago when human Digimon and beast Digimon

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:29.620
warred against each other.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.580
Their battle laid waste to the digital world, befouling what was once beautiful.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.140
But Lusamon appeared and brought an end to the fighting.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:43.010
For a time he ruled in peace, but soon he was corrupted by his own power.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.770
My, this story sure sounds familiar.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:46.530
Pokémon?

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:47.130
What?

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:52.230
The ten legendary warriors arose to free the oppressed and abused Digimon.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:55.930
They battled valiantly, and after a fierce struggle,

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:59.420
they were able to defeat the tyrannical Lusamon.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:07.760
After peace was restored to the digital world, champions were chosen to protect that peace.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.840
Terubimon, Ofanimon, and myself.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.460
But as before, our time of harmony was short-lived.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:19.460
Terubimon wanted to control the digital world by himself, and so attacked me.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.630
You know the rest of the story, thanks to Sorcerer-mon.

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.890
Ofanimon rescued me and brought me to safety here,

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:29.850
where I have slumbered and regained my strength until I was awakened by you,

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.020
Legendary warriors.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.160
Luckily, you came just when we needed Serafiman most.

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.020
The digital world is in a crisis, as you can see.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:43.710
A digital world looks like Swiss cheese.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.470
And the future looks even more bleak.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.270
You see, Cherubiman has sent his minions to destroy it.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.250
This is even more serious than I'd imagine.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:52.270
We must find Ophaniman at once.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.250
Yes, my lord.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.830
Your combined might can surely defeat Cherubiman.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.560
And of course, you'll have my help.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.770
While you've slept, I felt that I have too.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:03.370
and I have dreamt only of fighting at your side against that evil creature.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:07.240
Dear brave Sorcerer Mon, you are a true friend.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:10.480
Thank you. Your courage gives me strength.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:12.280
I am as you taught me.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:14.560
And I must thank you for your courage.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.960
All would be lost were it not for you.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:20.700
But now I must ask that you do one more favor for me.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:24.180
Before the fighting begins, go back to your own world.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:28.300
Your task is done, and it's too dangerous for you to stay.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.880
But we're legendary warriors.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.260
Yeah, we can't just walk away now.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:36.100
Good.

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.160
Hope Rat Brigade here.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.440
And ready to fight.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:43.860
You better be, cause me introduce other Digimon who defeat you.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.010
Ranamon.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.190
Charmed, I'm sure.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:47.560
Arbormon.

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.840
You're in for it now, right?

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.220
And lastly, Mercurymon.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:57.220
So these be the whelps who hast given thee so much trouble? Pathetic.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.900
Well, thee tougher than look.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:12:59.900
Verily.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:05.320
It will be utter delight to defeat thee, and to hand Seraphimon another drubbing in Cherubimon's name.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.860
With so many options, I don't know where to start.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.120
Enough of your meaningless taunts. Tell me where Ophanimon is, now!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:16.560
Me no care about her, me just want this spirit back, so give it!

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.980
Why don't you come get it, buddy? Yeah!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:19.820
Yeah!

00:14:02.652 --> 00:14:04.652
Thanks for watching!

00:14:06.524 --> 00:14:08.524
Thanks for watching!

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:27.420
turned show him or two oh well did and now i show you thing or three sure you don't want to get warmed up

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:36.400
Well, just shoot at the floor, sugar.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:37.660
Thunder!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.390
Whelming lesson in combat.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.700
Let me show you how it's done!

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.010
Groundhouse Power!

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:06.770
You go get your big spirit, Rockhead.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:07.410
Fetch.

00:16:08.290 --> 00:16:11.390
Be careful or you'll get smashed next when I'm on.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:12.470
Grumblemon, no!

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:13.790
You cannot do this!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.150
I beg your pardon?

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.310
You shall not lead us down the path of ruin.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:20.270
I've waited a lifetime to see peace restored to the digital world,

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.390
and you're not going to stop it from returning!

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:23.920
Crystal Barrage!

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:29.960
Now on to four Dark Reflections!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.020
Sorsima!

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:34.800
Worry not, my lord!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:35.790
Huh?

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:39.500
Retio!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.660
Of the seven stars!

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:05.750
Please, I ask again that you return to your world and leave this to me.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.330
There's no way we'll leave.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.300
Yeah, even if we wanted to, we don't know how.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:14.410
I can't fight them and keep you safe. You must go.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:19.520
Are you kidding? You can't fight all those guys by yourself.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.420
I mean, come on, you just woke up.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.360
You need us.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.990
This foolish compassion be his weakness.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.030
Attack the humans and keep him distracted.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:29.970
We should be...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.380
fighting them fine by us we fight you good

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:10.740
No! Into a digi-egg!

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:14.610
How ironic.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.850
Seraphimon sought to defeat Cherubimon,

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.770
but now his fractal code shall be used for our ends.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:20.990
No, it can't be!

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:23.090
The hope of the digital world is gone!

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:24.540
No, it's not!

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:29.830
Maybe we can bring him back if we have his egg, right, Sorcerimon?

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:33.550
Yes! We must protect that egg at all costs!

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.430
Oh, thou shan't get far, trust me.

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:40.400
If we can get the egg to Ofanimon, she may be able to revive Serafimon.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.520
All right, go get it!

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:44.900
Be not stupid!

